<title>USA: Some US cash DAP prices fall on waning demand.</title>
<headline>Some US cash DAP prices fall on waning demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some U.S. cash diammonium phosphate (DAP) values were lower Wednesday on weak demand and ammonia prices were flat, cash sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no demand,&quot; said one DAP dealer. &quot;China's dropped out of the market and the U.S. season hadn't begun yet.&quot;</p>
<p>Ammonia dealers reported light application of ammonia between rain storms in Texas.</p>
<p>			  Dlrs/short ton	 Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	  176-178		     unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf    186-188		     dn 1</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	  220-225		     unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
